           <div class="blog-body">
             <h1 class="blog-title mb-4">Srinivasa Ramanujan: A Self-Taught Mathematical Genius</h1>
             <p class="lead">Srinivasa Ramanujan is known worldwide for his genius and extraordinary contributions to mathematics. His discoveries in mathematics have profoundly reshaped the subject, leaving an indelible mark on the world of numbers and theories.</p>

             <div class="section-title mt-5">Ramanujan's Extraordinary Contributions</div>
             <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                 <p>✅ Made invaluable contributions to number theory, infinite series, and mathematical formulas.</p>
                 <p>✅ Developed over 3,900 mathematical formulas and theorems throughout his career.</p>
                 <p>✅ Discovered the infinite series formula for pi in 1914, a significant achievement.</p>
             </div>

             <div class="highlight-text">
                 Remarkably, Srinivasa Ramanujan never received any formal education in mathematics. It was his unparalleled interest and innate talent in the subject that made him famous throughout the world.
             </div>

             <div class="section-title mt-5">Celebrating National Mathematics Day</div>
             <p>Every year, December 22nd is celebrated as National Mathematics Day in India. This day commemorates the birth anniversary of Srinivasa Ramanujan, serving as an occasion to honor his achievements and inspire future generations in the field of mathematics.</p>

             <div class="section-title mt-5">Early Life and Challenges</div>
             <div class="benefit-item">
               <div class="benefit-title">1. A Childhood Spent in Poverty</div>
               <div class="benefit-content">
                 Srinivasa Ramanujan was born on December 22, 1887, into a modest family in Tamil Nadu, India. His childhood was marked by extreme poverty, a significant challenge that limited his opportunities for formal education.
               </div>
             </div>
             <div class="benefit-item">
               <div class="benefit-title">2. Educational Struggles Due to Mathematical Passion</div>
               <div class="benefit-content">
                 Despite his intellectual brilliance, Ramanujan's overwhelming interest in mathematics led him to neglect other subjects. This singular focus ultimately caused him to fail in other areas and drop out of college, highlighting his deep commitment to the world of numbers.
               </div>
             </div>

             <div class="section-title mt-5">Unwavering Interest in Mathematics</div>
             <p>Srinivasa Ramanujan is remembered worldwide for his remarkable contributions to mathematics. Despite his family's severe financial difficulties, he never compromised on his circumstances or his dreams. Driven by an insatiable curiosity, he independently read numerous mathematical books, discovered countless new mathematical formulas, and conducted his own profound experiments in mathematics, showcasing the power of self-taught genius.</p>

           </div>
         </div>
   </div>

            
